## 14. To Arthur and Eric

Ceptr asked computing to be receptive: to receive the carrier before the symbol, to make room for meaning to arrive, to
let coherence hold among peers who each keep their own copy of the agreements. Every construct it named for that
purpose has a construction here under the same name, and what it intended each to guarantee is a statement with a
proof. The work began in the right place; this is what it looks like with the mathematics in hand.
